From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kholin <oodzchen@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 11:38:30 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: qcom: qdsp6: set drvdata before registering clocks

q6dsp_clock_dev_probe() exposes the LPASS clocks through
devm_clk_hw_register() and devm_of_clk_add_hw_provider() before calling
dev_set_drvdata(dev, cc).

If another driver probing in parallel (such as lpass-va-macro requesting
LPASS_CLK_ID_VA_CORE_MCLK) resolves a clock and calls clk_prepare_enable()
during the window after devm_of_clk_add_hw_provider() and before
dev_set_drvdata(), clk_q6dsp_prepare() / clk_vote_q6dsp_block() reads
dev_get_drvdata(clk->dev) == NULL and dereferences cc->desc (offset 0x348
on 64-bit). Because clk_prepare_enable() holds the global clk_prepare_lock
mutex across ops->prepare(), the resulting Oops leaves clk_prepare_lock
permanently locked and stalls the rest of boot.

Set dev_set_drvdata(dev, cc) as soon as cc is populated, before registering
any clock hardware or the OF clock provider.

Co-Authored-By: Antigravity <noreply@deepmind.google>
---
 sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6dsp-lpass-clocks.c | 3 +--
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6dsp-lpass-clocks.c b/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6dsp-lpass-clocks.c
index 03838582a..9b88a3ba0 100644
--- a/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6dsp-lpass-clocks.c
+++ b/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6dsp-lpass-clocks.c
@@ -144,6 +144,7 @@ int q6dsp_clock_dev_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 
 	cc->desc = desc;
 	cc->dev = dev;
+	dev_set_drvdata(dev, cc);
 	q6dsp_clks = desc->clks;
 
 	for (i = 0; i < desc->num_clks; i++) {
@@ -178,8 +179,6 @@ int q6dsp_clock_dev_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 	if (ret)
 		return ret;
 
-	dev_set_drvdata(dev, cc);
-
 	return 0;
 }
 EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(q6dsp_clock_dev_probe);
-- 
